The strand that presides is the one with the authority to decide what happens next.

Your own name for yourself can govern what you choose. The name others know you by can govern what they invite you into, what they trust you with, and what they let you put down. In a relationship, the history you’ve lived together often has more authority than either person’s account of it.

Take the strong one. You might have stopped calling yourself that years ago. If everyone still brings you their burdens and nobody thinks to ask about yours, that name still presides in the room. The braid starts to turn when you ask for help and somebody comes. Now there’s a shared memory that can change what strong affords you.

For the Pantheon, I’d ask which name gets to interpret the next act? If you say no and they hear betrayal, the old name still has authority. If they can hear a boundary and keep you close, the relationship has room for who you’re becoming.